{"Backup-code branch bypasses TOTP requirement when disabling 2FA - the handler accepts backupCode as an alternate path that runs before TOTP validation and doesn't require a valid TOTP code, allowing any authenticated session with password to disable 2FA using a backup code": 0.12369697540998459, "Used backup code is never invalidated when disabling 2FA, allowing a stolen code to be reused until the account is reconfigured": 0.08486348390579224, "Backup codes are persisted to database during setup before 2FA is actually enabled, creating a data-model lifecycle mismatch where backup codes exist for accounts not yet protected by 2FA": 0.40786418318748474, "Backup-code login submit button lacks isSubmitting guard, allowing double-click or Enter-key repeat to send two credential requests before first response returns, causing spurious IncorrectBackupCode errors": 0.43742260336875916, "Backup codes can be reused indefinitely during login - the authorizeCredentials path sets matched entry to null but the code may remain accepted depending on how the array is interpreted later": 0.16959074139595032, "Stale backup-code download URL may point to old code set - opening modal multiple times can leave prior object URLs alive because cleanup is not tied to backupCodesUrl changes in effect lifecycle": 0.6304736137390137, "2FA enable flow no longer calls onEnable when 2FA is actually enabled on server - callback is now delayed until modal is dismissed instead of immediately after server returns 200": 0.8449874520301819, "Mode switching between TwoFactor and BackupCode can leave stale totpCode/backupCode values in submitted form, causing hidden leftover backup code to override visible TOTP entry due to auth layer preferring credentials.backupCode when present": 0.7950356006622314}